# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere...
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except under vendor/, which is left completely alone.
#
# Every file in vendor/ has its sha384 recorded in vendor/INTEGRITY.txt and was
# checked byte-identical against upstream. Git's autocrlf would rewrite the
# text ones to CRLF on checkout under Windows, which changes their bytes and
# breaks that match — the provenance record would then be quietly wrong for
# anyone who cloned on the wrong platform. `-text` disables conversion in both
# directions so what is committed is exactly what is served.
vendor/** -text

*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
